hadiths[35]{hadithnumber,text}:
"778","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Wear some of your white clothes; For it is among your best clothes, and shroud your dead in it.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"779","On the authority of Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Wear white, for it is purer and more pleasant, and shroud your dead in it.” [Narrated by Al-Nasa’i and Al-Hakim]"
"780","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was of medium stature. I saw him wearing a red mantle. I have never seen anything more graceful than that. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"781","On the authority of Abu Juhaifah Wahb bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) in Mecca, and he was in a red tent made of red leather, so Bilal came out with his ablution, and then Bilal gave the call to prayer, so the Prophet (ﷺ) came out wearing a red robe, as if I was looking at the whites of his legs, so he performed ablution and Bilal’s ear, so I started following his mouth here and there, as he turned his head right and left: Hail to the prayer, Come to success, then a spear was fixed for him, so he came forward and prayed, the dog and the donkey passing in front of him without being prevented. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"782","On the authority of Abu Rimtha Rifa’ah Al-Taymi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wearing two green garments. [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"783","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Makkah on the day of its conquest and he was wearing a black turban. [Muslim] ."
"784","On the authority of Abu Saeed Amr bin Harith, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wearing a black turban, the two ends of which have fallen between his shoulders. [Muslim] And in his narration: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed the people, wearing a black turban."
"785","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was shrouded in three white sahulli robes made of linen, without a shirt or turban. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"786","On her authority, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out one morning, wearing a black hair cloak. [Muslim]"
"787","On the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey one night, and he said to me: “Do you have any water?” I said: Yes, so he got off his mount and walked until he disappeared in the black of the night. Then he came and I poured water from the container over him, so he washed his face while wearing a woolen cloak on him, but he could not remove his arms from it until he took them out from the bottom of the cloak. So he washed his arms and wiped his head, then I leaned over to remove his socks and said: “Leave them, for I brought them in pure” and wiped them. (Agreed upon) And in a narration: he was wearing a Syrian robe with tight sleeves. And in a narration: This incident occurred in the Battle of Tabuk."
"788","On the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The most beloved garment to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the shirt. [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"789","On the authority of Asmaa bint Yazid Al-Ansariyya, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The sleeve of the shirt of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) reached to the wrist. [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"790","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \Whoever allows his lower garment to drag out of vanity will find that Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" On this Abu Bakr (May Allah be pleased with him) replied: \""O Messenger of Allah! My lower garment keeps sliding down though I take care to pull it and wrap it.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""You are not of those who do it out of vanity.\"" [Al- Bukhari] ."""
"791","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \On the Day of Resurrection"," Allah will not look at him who trails his lower garment out of pride.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"792","On the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whatever of the garment is below the ankles is in the Fire.” [Al-Bukhari]"
"793","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, \There are three to whom Allah will neither speak on the Day of Resurrection nor will look at them nor purify them (i.e."," of their sins)"," and they will be severely tormented.\"" When he repeated this (statement) thrice"," Abu Dharr (May Allah be pleased with him) said: \""They are doomed and destroyed! (But) who are they"," O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said"," \""One whose lower garment trails"," one who boasts of kindness shown to another; and one who promotes sale of his business by taking false oaths.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"794","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Isbal is the garment, the shirt, and the turban. Whoever drags something out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud and Al-Nasa’i]"
"795","On the authority of Abu Jarir Jaber bin Salim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw a man whose opinion people followed; He does not say anything unless they come from him; I said: Who is this? They said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah - twice. He said: “Do not say peace be upon you, peace be upon you. The greeting of the dead” - I said: Peace be upon you. He will remove it from you, and if you are in a drought or a wasteland, and your camel is lost, then you call him to return it to you.” He said: I said: “Entrust it to me.” He said: “Do not insult anyone.” He said: “I have not harmed any free man, slave, camel, or sheep after him.” And do not despise any kindness, and speak to your brother with your face open to him And raise your garment to half the shin, and if you refuse, then to the ankles, and beware of letting the garment slip, for it is from pride, and Allah does not like imagination, and if someone insults you and reproaches you, for what he knows about you, do not criticize him for what you know about him, for that will only harm him.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"796","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: While a man was praying with his garment drawn down, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: “Go and perform ablution.” So he went and performed ablution, then he came and said: “Go and perform ablution.” A man said, O Messenger of Allah, why did you order him to perform ablution and then he remained silent about it? He said: “He was praying while his garment was drawn down, and Allah does not accept the prayer of a man whose lower garment is trailing.” [Abu Dawud]"
"797","On the authority of Qais bin Bishr al-Taghlabi, he said: My father - who was a companion of Abu Darda’ - told me that he said: In Damascus there was a man from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) called Sahl bin Al-Hanzaliyya, and he was a solitary man who rarely sat with people. It will harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a squadron and it came. A man from among them came and sat in the council where the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting. He said to a man next to him: If you saw us when we and the enemy met, and so-and-so picked up and was stabbed, and said: Take it from me, and I am the forgiving boy. What do you think of his statement? He said: I do not see him except that his reward has been nullified. Then another heard of that. He said: I do not see anything wrong with that, so they disputed until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard and said: “Glory be to Allah? There is no harm in him being rewarded and praised.” I saw Abu Darda’ being pleased with that, and he started raising his head to him and saying: Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? Then he said: Yes. He continued repeating it until I say, let him kneel down. He said: Another day passed by us, and Al-Darda’ said to him: A word that will benefit us and will not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to us: “The one who spends on good is like one who extends his hand in charity and does not take it away.” Then another day passed by us, and Abu Al-Darda’ said to him: A word that will benefit us and will not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah said: May Allah’s (ﷺ): “What a wonderful man, Khurraym al-Asadi! Were it not for the length of his robe and the sheer length of his garment!” Then he reached Khurraym, and he made up. He took a blade with it and cut his robe up to his ears, and raised his garment to half of its stems. Then he passed by us another day, and Abu Darda’ said to him: A word that will benefit us and will not harm you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Allah, upon him be peace, says: “You are coming to meet your brothers, so prepare your saddlebags and dress so that you are like a mole among the people, for Allah does not like obscenity or obscenity.” [Abu Dawud]"
"798","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \The lower garment of a believer should be half way below the knees. He is guilty of no sin if they are up to the ankles. That which is below the ankles is in the Fire (of Hell). Allah will not look at one who allows his lower garment to trail out of vanity. [Abu Dawud] ."""
"799","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and there was a loose garment in my garment. He said: “O Abdullah, raise your garment.” So I raised it. Then he said: “Increase,” so I increased, and I have continued to observe it. Some of the people said: Where to? He said: To the middle of the legs. [Muslim]."
"800","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” Umm Salamah said: “So what should women do with their lower garments?” He said: “They should be slackened by a span.” She said: “Then their feet would be exposed.” He said: “So they should relax it an arm’s length and not add more.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud) And Al-Tirmidhi]"
"801","On the authority of Muadh bin Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever abandons clothing out of humility to Allah, and he is able to do so, Allah will call him on the Day of Resurrection above the heads of creation until He gives him the choice of which garment of faith he wishes to wear.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"802","On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah loves to see the effect of His grace on His servant.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"803","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Do not wear silk (clothes). For whoever wears (them) in this life will be deprived of them in the Hereafter.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"804","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Only those who have no share in the Hereafter wear silk.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] And in a narration by Al-Bukhari: “He who has no share in the Hereafter.”"
"805","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the afterlife.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"806","I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) holding a piece of gold in his left hand and a silk (cloth) in his right hand. Then he said, \These two are forbidden for the males of my Ummah.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"807","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Wearing silk and gold is forbidden for the males of my nation, and permissible for their females.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"808","On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade us from drinking from gold and silver vessels, from eating from them, from wearing silk and brocade, and from sitting on them. [Al-Bukhari]"
"809","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) permitted Zubair and `Abdur-Rahman bin `Auf (May Allah be pleased with them) to wear silk because they were suffering from an itch. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"810","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Do not ride on saddles made from silk or leopard's skin.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"811","On the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the skins of wild beasts. [Narrated by Abu Dawud, Al-Tirmidhi, and Al-Nasa’i] And in a narration by Al-Tirmidhi: He forbade the skins of lions to be spread out. "
"812","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) acquired a new garment, and would identify it by its name—whether a turban, a shirt, or a robe—he would say: “O Allah, praise be to You. You have clothed me. I ask You for its goodness and the goodness of what was made for it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what was made for it.” [Abu Dawud] Hassan)."
